# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Kobbi's Oven Next.js website following the official Vercel documentation.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Documentation Retrieved
Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart to ensure using the most up-to-date implementation approach.

### 2. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version compatible with Next.js 16.3.4)
- Used npm as the package manager (existing package-lock.json identified)
- Added 384 packages with no vulnerabilities detected

### 3. Code Changes

#### Modified Files:

**website/package.json**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies

**website/package-lock.json**
- Updated with new dependency tree for @vercel/analytics

**website/src/app/layout.tsx**
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body section
- Follows Next.js App Router best practices by placing Analytics in the root layout

### 4. Framework-Specific Implementation
This project uses Next.js with the App Router pattern, so the Analytics component was added to:
- **File**: `src/app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
- **Location**: Inside the `<body>` tag, after all content components
- **Import**: Used the Next.js-specific import from `@vercel/analytics/next`

### 5. Verification Steps Completed
✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ TypeScript compilation passed
✅ Static pages generated (9/9 routes)
✅ Linter ran successfully (no errors in modified files)
✅ Pre-existing lint issues in other files remain unchanged

### 6. Next Steps for Deployment
To complete the Vercel Web Analytics setup:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after users visit the site

## Files Changed
- `website/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `website/package-lock.json` - Updated lock file with new dependencies
- `website/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component to root layout

## Notes
- The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router
- No existing functionality was affected
- All code style and formatting conventions were preserved
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views and visitor data once deployed to Vercel
